        <body>
            <div xml:id="d440">

                <pb facs="0577" n="475" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg475"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 13837/2.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                    Dodge.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-06-04"><hi rendition="#italic">June 4,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Bacon acknowledges his telegram of June 3, and requests him to advise
                    department immediately upon the arrest of Bailey and <pb facs="0578" n="476"
                        xml:id="pg476"/> detention of the <hi rendition="#italic">Goldsboro</hi>.
                    Mr. Bacon instructs Mr. Dodge to ascertain what formalities the Honduranean
                    Government will require before turning Bailey and the vessel over to the United
                    States Government.</p>
            </div>
